3. THEORETICAL ARCHITECTURE OF THE LUNAR RESOURCE ECONOMY

The corrected results naturally yield a four‑layered architecture:

Layer 1: Physical Resource Kernel. A dynamic system described by the mass‑energy balances and closure‑ratio investment functions. The state evolution follows the differential inclusions of Axiom 4a or the SDE of Axiom 4b, with the optimal closure policy from Theorem 2.1 and spares from 2.2.

Layer 2: Adaptive Control Plane. A set of model predictive controllers using only Lipschitz‑continuous approximators (Theorem 2.4) for deterministic and stochastic regimes. These controllers solve a relaxed RCIP at each control interval; stability under delay is mathematically guaranteed within the derived \tau_{\max}.

Layer 3: Governance Core. The VCG‑with‑post‑fairness mechanism of Theorem 2.3 runs on a periodic basis. The core property (Theorem 2.5) assures coalitional stability. Ambiguity‑robust variants from 2.6 can be activated when facing deep uncertainty.

Layer 4: Cislunar Treaty Compliance. A formal model of extraction‑right exchanges as a directed acyclic graph, with consistency proofs now including a mapping to the semantic obligations of the Artemis Accords, represented as a set of deontic constraints. Compliance is provable under the assumption of honest graph updates; a future integration with multi‑agent commitment protocols is outlined but not implemented.

