4. THE LUNAR RESOURCE ECONOMIST — A THEORETICIAN’S ROLE (REFINED)

The Lunar Resource Economist remains a theoretical systems steward, but the role now includes rigorous sensitivity analysis and explicit fragility quantification. The job consists of:

· Proving theorems under clearly separated disturbance regimes, with computable bounds on delay margins, Lipschitz constants, and distributional radii.
· Deriving mechanisms that are provably DSIC by construction, using established characterisation theorems.
· Constructing symbolic models that link Wright’s‑law learning to cooperative game properties.
· Producing fragility certificates alongside every optimal policy to warn future implementers of the conditions under which the guarantees fail.
· Acknowledging that every theorem is contingent on its axioms; the role includes clearly demarcating which axioms require empirical validation before the theory can be applied to a physical settlement.

No fieldwork, empirical testing, or code training is undertaken in this doctoral program. However, the theoretical work is structured so that each theorem outputs a testable condition that an experimental program can later verify or falsify.

