Appendix H. Behavioral Extensions (Theoretical)

To account for bounded rationality, we present a model where agents may panic under resource stress, causing their reported utility to deviate from the true u_i by a random distortion. We prove a robustness result: if the distortion is bounded in sup‑norm, the VCG mechanism with a slight modification (adding a “safety margin” to the survival thresholds) maintains an approximate DSIC property (\epsilon-incentive compatibility). The proof uses the concept of ex‑post regret and the Lipschitz continuity of the allocation rule. Full derivations are deferred to a specialized course module.

